# Python bytecode: regenerated on every run, and machine-specific, so it must never be
# published. The plugin package is meant to be readable and reproducible, not to carry
# build residue from whoever last ran it.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo

# Runtime state must never be committed. The plugin's state lives outside the package
# (~/.kaggle-agent and ~/.kaggle-cli), but a stray local run can still drop one here.
#
# Every pattern below is ANCHORED to the package root with a leading slash, and that is
# load-bearing rather than cosmetic. A pattern with no internal separator — `handoff/`,
# `sources/`, `plots/` — matches at *any* depth, so an unanchored `handoff/` silently
# excluded `skills/handoff/SKILL.md`: a skill the manifest declares, the relationship
# graph references, and the collab category links to. The package passed all 842 checks,
# because every one of them reads the working tree and the file was sitting right there on
# disk; only the repository was short a skill. A published package that fails to import is
# exactly the failure this file is supposed to prevent, so the rules stay anchored and
# `tools/check_plugin.py` asserts that no manifest path is gitignored.
presence.json
log-monitor.json
search-engine.json
config.json
credentials.json
/handoff/
/sources/
/plots/
*.tmp

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
